--[[--
Gaussian Splatting DragDrop Addon for Resolve/Fusion
Created By: Andrew Hazelden <andrew@andrewhazelden.com>
Date Created: 2025-08-27
Last Updated: 2026-10-31 12.29 PM

## Overview

The "Gaussian Splatting DragDrop.fu" file is a Resolve/Fusion add-on that allows you to drag and drop .ply files from your desktop folder browsing window into the Fusion nodes view area. The 3DGS asset is automatically added to the composite and is ready for use.

The .fu file works by adding a new "Irrealix GaussianSplatting" OpenFX node to the active foreground Fusion page composite when a drag and drop event occurs. The PLY filepath information from the drag and drop loaded document is then added to the GaussianSplatting node's "Model 1" section.

This approach saves time and effort compared to constantly futzing around with file open dialogs, and navigating to the exact deeply nested filepath you require, when you want to load a new 3DGS .ply model into the Fusion node graph/viewport.

## Requirements

In order to have access to the GaussianSplatting node in the Fusion page, it requires the installation of the "Irrealix Gaussian Splatting plugin" that is available here:

https://aescripts.com/gaussian-splatting-for-davinci-resolve/

## DragDrop Addon Installation

Step 1. Copy the "Gaussian Splatting DragDrop.fu" file into the Fusion user preferences "Config" PathMap folder. You could also use the "Config" PathMap folder that exists at "Reactor:/Deploy/Config/" or "Lightfielder:/Resolve/Config/".

### Fusion Studio Install Location

	Windows Path:
	%AppData%\Blackmagic Design\Fusion\Config\

	Linux Path:
	$HOME/.fusion/BlackmagicDesign/Fusion/Config\

	MacOS Path:
	$HOME/Library/Application Support/Blackmagic Design/Fusion/Config/

### Resolve Studio Install Location

	Windows Path:
	%AppData%\Blackmagic Design\DaVinci Resolve\Fusion\Config\

	Linux Path:
	$HOME/.fusion/BlackmagicDesign/DaVinci Resolve/Fusion/Config/

	MacOS Path:
	$HOME/Library/Application Support/Blackmagic Design/DaVinci Resolve/Fusion/Config/

2. Relaunch Resolve Studio/Fusion Studio.

3. Add the GaussianSplatting node to the comp. With the GaussianSplatting node selected in the nodes view, navigate to the inspector window. If you have a commercial license of the GaussianSplatting plugin, now is a good time to enter your registration number using the node's Register window.

